{"name":"Egg Liqueur","hex":"#dccaa8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"egg","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food.","An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something).","To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egg"},{"term":"liqueur","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flavored alcoholic beverage that is usually very sweet and contains a high percentage of alcohol."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["to flavor or treat (wine) with a liqueur","to top up bottles of sparkling wine with a sugar solution"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liqueur"}],"entries":[{"title":"Advocaat","blocks":[{"text":"Advocaat or advocatenborrel is a traditional Dutch alcoholic beverage made from eggs, sugar, and brandy. The rich and creamy drink has a smooth, custard-like consistency. The typical alcohol content is generally between 14% and 20% ABV. Its contents may be a blend of egg yolks, aromatic spirits, sugar or honey, brandy, vanilla, and sometimes cream. Notable makers of advocaat include the Belgian and Dutch Filliers, Warninks, Bols, DeKuyper, Verpoorten and Croatian Darna Ovo Liker."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Advocaat_bottle_with_glass.jpg/330px-Advocaat_bottle_with_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advocaat"},{"title":"Egg","blocks":[{"text":"An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has developed enough to survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/330px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg"},{"title":"Liqueur","blocks":[{"text":"A liqueur or cordial is an alcoholic drink composed of spirits and additional flavorings such as sugar, fruits, herbs, and spices. Often served with or after dessert, they are typically heavily sweetened and un-aged, beyond a resting period during production, when necessary, for their flavors to mingle."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/92/Licor-Beir%C3%A3o-%26-Orus_-_Orus_Clothing_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liqueur"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Affiche_%27Advokaat%27_voor_stokerij_Vliegen%2C_Hasselt.jpg/500px-Affiche_%27Advokaat%27_voor_stokerij_Vliegen%2C_Hasselt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Affiche_%27Advokaat%27_voor_stokerij_Vliegen%2C_Hasselt.jpg/1280px-Affiche_%27Advokaat%27_voor_stokerij_Vliegen%2C_Hasselt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped